WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.927
A view can sit in the middle of a dependency chain.

00:00:02.927 --> 00:00:05.697
Base tables feed the shared interface.

00:00:05.697 --> 00:00:09.027
A report-specific CTE reads the view.

00:00:09.027 --> 00:00:11.842
A report consumes the final result.

00:00:11.842 --> 00:00:17.467
If the view grain or column meaning changes, every downstream layer may be affected.

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:22.952
Treat important shared views as versioned contracts, not disposable snippets.

00:00:22.952 --> 00:00:26.387
Reusable SQL objects create dependencies.

00:00:26.387 --> 00:00:33.092
Before changing a base view, identify which other views, reports, or applications depend on it.

00:00:33.092 --> 00:00:36.312
Good change management includes version awareness, tests,

00:00:36.312 --> 00:00:41.440
and communication—not just editing CREATE VIEW until it succeeds.
